  "worked_solution": "We want to find a \"path\" from $C$ to $B$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,c,$ and $d.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{CB}=\\overset{\\to }{CE}+\\overset{\\to }{EF}+\\overset{\\to }{FA}+\\overset{\\to }{AB}\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14212914/assets/18b8d39937dd23f03a030727e642729259ec5ab0c6fcb438c8bf82a2b7aaf08d.png)\n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{CE}=d,\\,\\overset{\\to }{EF}=-c,\\,\\overset{\\to }{FA}=b,\\,\\overset{\\to }{AB}=-a.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14212914/assets/6f1c084747ad1b0de2ab28979fee8e14db9463f1d82d07ab787581789bcb6e37.png)\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{CB} & =\\overset{\\to }{CE}+\\overset{\\to }{EF}+\\overset{\\to }{FA}+\\overset{\\to }{AB} \\\\  & =d-c+b-a.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
